                "content": "# PAJARO RIVER BASIN\n\n# 11-1542. UVAS CREEK NEAR GILROY, CALIF.\n\nLOCATION. -Lat 36\u00b059'35\", long 121\u00b034'20\", in Las Animas Grant, on left bank 400 ft upstream from county road bridge, 0.4 mile southwest of Gilroy, Santa Clara County, and 3.9 miles downstream from Bodfish Creek.\n\nDRAINAGE AREA.--71.2 sq mi.\n\nRECORDS AVAILABLE.--January 1959 to September 1968.\n\nGAGE --Digital water-stage recorder. Altitude of gage is 190 ft (from topographic map). Prior to Feb. 28, 1966, graphic water-stage recorder at same site and datum.\n\nAVERAGE DISCHARGE.--9 years, 30.2 cfs (21,860 acre-ft per year).\n\nEXTREMES Maximum discharge during year, 560 cfs Jan. 30 (gage height, 5.90 ft) ; no flow for many days. extended above 3,300 cfs; no flow for many days in each year. 1959-68: Maximum discharge, 9,490 cfs Feb. 1, 1963 (gage height, 17.66 ft), from rating curve\n\nREMARKS, Records good. Flow regulated by Uvas Reservoir (see sta. no. 11-1540.2.). Diversion above station for irrigation and municipal supply of city of Gilroy.\n\nREVISIONS (water year).--1967 report: 1963.\n\nDISCHARGE. IN CUBIC FEET PER SECOND, WATER YEAR OCTOBER 1967 TO SEPTEMBER 1968",
